From e7319e41d1bcc32b94bebbacce5d2b9ea65ed55e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:17:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: hub-cpu-alert uses the pre-lease advisory's
 10 s limit; PR #1856 review nits

The pre-lease advisory (hub_cpu_advisory) defers every claim on a sample older than
10 s, but kanban_hub_cpu_alert still called a sample fresh up to the locked gate's
15 s: a sampler stuck 10-15 s behind started nothing on the hub and never filed the
hub-cpu-advisory-stale card. Both now read kanban_admission.PRELEASE_MAX_AGE_MS
(RED first: a 12 s-old sample must trip the alert).

Review nits from #1856 (reviews 5885991227, 5886827276):
- hub_cpu_advisory docstring: stale is >10 s, not >15 s.
- _final_hub_gate docstring: back-to-back local claims in one sampler period share one
  pre-claim sample (only the max_in_progress census protects CPU between them); the
  independent re-sample was dropped deliberately (it overran the 2.25 s hold in the
  GIL-busy gateway -> hub_cpu_unknown after the lease).
- the waiting-turn comment no longer mentions a ~1 s sample.
- dispatch skip words: a claim_deferred detail from this host's admission gate
  (hub_cpu_*, hub_admission_overrun, hub_capacity_full) says "this host's admission
  gate deferred its claim" instead of "the Board".
- tests: limit_unknown stage covered; the contention test is renamed, its cm.sample
  stub fails instead of advancing the clock and its bound allows one census
  (HUB_BOARDS * 8); the sampler-read claim test's docstring matches what it runs.
